        "sender": "Elizabeth",
        "date": "1845-03-20",
        "approximate": false,
        "dateLabel": "20 March 1845",
        "text": "The old gods are dethroned.",
        "note": "",
        "callbacks": []
      },
      {
        "snippetId": "s686",
        "messageOrdinal": 30,
        "sender": "Robert",
        "date": "1845-05-24",
        "approximate": false,
        "dateLabel": "24 May 1845",
        "text": "But I never mind what I am told!",
        "note": "",
        "callbacks": []
      },
      {
        "snippetId": "s2010",
        "messageOrdinal": 135,
        "sender": "Robert",
        "date": "1845-10-23",
        "approximate": false,
        "dateLabel": "23 October 1845",
        "text": "But I must answer you, and be forgiven, too, dearest.",
        "note": "",
        "callbacks": []
      },
      {
        "snippetId": "s4061",
        "messageOrdinal": 221,
        "sender": "Elizabeth",
        "date": "1846-02-05",
        "approximate": false,
        "dateLabel": "5 February 1846",
        "text": "Dear Miss Mitford comes to-morrow, and I am not glad enough.",
        "note": "",
        "callbacks": []
      },
      {
        "snippetId": "s4410",
        "messageOrdinal": 239,
        "sender": "Elizabeth",
        "date": "1846-02-20",
        "approximate": false,
        "dateLabel": "20 February 1846",
        "text": "What makes you take them to be so bad, I suppose, is just feeling in them how near we are.",
        "note": "",
        "callbacks": []
      },
      {
        "snippetId": "s6246",
        "messageOrdinal": 316,
        "sender": "Elizabeth",
        "date": "1846-04-17",
        "approximate": false,
        "dateLabel": "17 April 1846",
        "text": "So you ‘felt’ that I was down-stairs to-day!",
        "note": "",
        "callbacks": []
      },
      {
        "snippetId": "s7791",
        "messageOrdinal": 387,
        "sender": "Elizabeth",
        "date": "1846-06-03",
        "approximate": false,
        "dateLabel": "3 June 1846",
        "text": "And this is the earnest thing of all ... that I love you as I can love—and am for ever ... living and dying....",
        "note": "",
        "callbacks": []
      },
      {
        "snippetId": "s8626",
        "messageOrdinal": 422,
        "sender": "Robert",
        "date": "1846-06-26",
        "approximate": false,
        "dateLabel": "26 June 1846",
        "text": "I will tell you something I meant to speak of yesterday.",
        "note": "",
        "callbacks": []
      },
      {
        "snippetId": "s9387",
        "messageOrdinal": 455,
        "sender": "Elizabeth",
        "date": "1846-07-14",
        "approximate": false,
        "dateLabel": "14 July 1846",
        "text": "I think I will let you beg my pardon; you unjust, dearest....",
        "note": "",
        "callbacks": []
      }
    ]
